  {
   "correction": "The duties do not run with the rounded 0.670. For a measured cell, core's duty takes the titration's carbon share, 0.6697790 at P200 (the regenerated records' skids.B.carbon_share_duty and measured_state.co_ion_carbon_share); only `cheme process cell` reports the membrane block's 0.670 (DESIGN.md D-010). The same statement is in tests/skid_formulas.py (stated_co_ion_carbon_fraction, hand_values), which compute the hand values at 0.670.",
   "effect": "The frozen E2 and E3 hand values carry a one-signed bias against the regenerated ones, inside every frozen tolerance: Skid A's exact volume -1.3e-4 relative (1165.15 L against 1165.30 L), the Skid B bleed -3.3e-4 (1.86608 L/h against 1.86670 L/h, a third of E3's rel 1e-3), the dose -2.2e-4 (2.09589 mol/h against 2.09635 mol/h). The values and tolerances stand.",
   "id": "X-1",
   "item": "measurements.co_ion_split",
   "statement": "process/cells.yaml membrane.co_ion_crossover HCO3- 0.670 (the P200 titration mean 0.6698 rounded): the split the duties run with"
  },
  {
   "correction": "Owner decision of 2026-11-06 (DESIGN.md D-058): Skid A's trip I-101 acts at pH 12.2, 0.2 above the criterion pH 12 of D-003, and T-101 is sized to reach the trip value at H, so that the trip has a margin for the probe's error and the campaign still lasts H at the measured WDE. The criterion pH 12 stays the reported stability criterion (process/design-basis.yaml threshold.ph); the sizing and trip value is the new key threshold.trip.ph 12.2, which scripts/regen.py step 3 writes into every duty (D-B and the comparison duties too: I-201 already tripped at 12.2).",
   "effect": "Skid A's reservoir grows 0.9 % (about 10 L of 1 M KOH) and its tank by 3 mm in diameter and 4 mm in height; the frozen E2, E4 and E10 items below move by less than their frozen tolerance except the E10 Skid A routes (rel 1e-6), which is why the tests compare with the superseding values. E1, E3, E5 to E9 and the other E10 items do not depend on the threshold. inputs.charge_per_carbon_ph12 and inputs.usable_hydroxide_mol_l stay the values at the criterion pH 12 (they are inputs, never compared with a regenerated value).",
   "id": "X-2",
   "item": "design.threshold_ph",
   "statement": "design threshold_ph: 12 (the duties run to the stability criterion pH 12 and T-101 is sized to reach it at H)"
  }
